{"ref":"BDB, מִיָּמִן","hw":"מִיָּמִן","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מִיָּמִן</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מִיָּמִין</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מִנְיָמִן</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מִנְיָמִין</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. </strong><br><strong>1.</strong>  priestly name: <strong>a.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">מִיָּמִן</span> assigned to David’s time, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 24:9\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.24.9\">1 Ch 24:9</a>. <strong>b.</strong>  Neh.’s time <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 10:8\" href=\"/Nehemiah.10.8\">Ne 10:8</a> = <span dir=\"rtl\">מִנְיָמִין</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:17\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.17\">12:17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:41\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.41\">41</a>. <strong>c.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">מִנְיָמִן</span> assigned to Hezekiah’s time <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 31:15\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.31.15\">2 Ch 31:15</a>. <strong>d.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">מִיָּמִין</span> went up with Zerub. <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:5\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.5\">Ne 12:5</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  one of those who took strange wives <a data-ref=\"Ezra 10:25\" href=\"/Ezra.10.25\">Ezr 10:25</a>.—𝔊 Βενιαμειν and (especially A 𝔊L) Μιαμειν.","next":"BDB, מין","prev":"BDB, מַ֫וִם"}